  "narrative": "The new batch is dominated by well-behaved null and near-null control analyses, and it strengthens the internal credibility of the already accepted dataset-specific associations rather than adding new large effects. All estimates are already signed to the claim direction. H26 is the TP53-loss specificity control for POLR2A: signed estimate -0.014, 95% CI -0.034 to +0.006, n=406/1594. The point is about 5% of the POLR2A mean magnitude and is statistically compatible with zero; I reject it as an unsupported meaningful TP53-loss/POLR2A association and close it. This supports, though it does not prove, that the accepted TP53-loss/USP7 effect is not simply a global screen or essentiality shift. H27-H31 test context dependence. H27 USP7-by-KRAS interaction (+0.018, CI -0.152 to +0.188), H28 SMARCA2-by-ARID1A-loss interaction (+0.037, CI -0.015 to +0.089), H29 STAT3-by-PIK3CA interaction (+0.001, CI -0.150 to +0.152), H30 WRN-by-adenocarcinoma interaction (-0.021, CI -0.085 to +0.042), and H31 NFE2L2-by-STK11-loss interaction (-0.026, CI -0.079 to +0.026) all have point estimates below the roughly 10% clinical-scale criterion and include zero. I reject each as unsupported evidence for meaningful modification in this dataset, while noting that some subgroup intervals are wide and therefore do not establish precise absence of heterogeneity. H32-H37 are predictor-specificity controls. SMARCA4 loss or PTEN loss do not affect USP7 dependency (H32: -0.002; H33: -0.005). SMARCA4 loss does not affect WRN dependency (H34: +0.003), PTEN loss does not meaningfully affect SMARCA2 dependency (H35: +0.018, about 4% of the SMARCA2 mean), SMARCA4 loss does not affect NFE2L2 dependency (H36: -0.012), and KEAP1 loss does not affect WRN dependency (H37: +0.007). These controls are near null on the scale of the accepted effects, so they reduce concern that accepted associations reflect broad cell-state or technical confounding and increase the apparent predictor specificity of accepted H6, H7, H11, H17, and H24 within this dataset. I am requesting independent validation of H7 (MSI-high and dependency_WRN) because it is a large accepted effect in a relatively small MSI-high subgroup, and independent stability would make it a more reliable dataset-specific claim. No new causal or external-generalizability claim is made.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 3 appraise update. Accepted dataset-specific active claims remain: H6 SMARCA4 loss -> stronger SMARCA2 dependency; H7 MSI-high -> stronger WRN dependency (independent validation now requested); H11 PTEN loss -> stronger STAT3 dependency; H17 KEAP1 loss -> weaker/less-negative NFE2L2 dependency; H24 TP53 loss -> weaker/less-negative USP7 dependency, already validated. New batch H26-H37 produced no new supported association. Rejected/closed as unsupported meaningful effects: H26 TP53 loss/POLR2A specificity control; H27 USP7 TP53-by-KRAS interaction; H28 SMARCA2 SMARCA4-by-ARID1A interaction; H29 STAT3 PTEN-by-PIK3CA interaction; H30 WRN MSI-by-lineage subtype interaction; H31 NFE2L2 KEAP1-by-STK11 interaction; H32 USP7 SMARCA4 cross-control; H33 USP7 PTEN cross-control; H34 WRN SMARCA4 cross-control; H35 SMARCA2 PTEN cross-control; H36 NFE2L2 SMARCA4 cross-control; H37 WRN KEAP1 cross-control. These nulls strengthen predictor specificity for accepted associations but are not formal equivalence proofs because some interaction intervals are wide. Next: assess H7 validation when delivered; if confirmed, prioritize validation of H6 and/or H17/H11 if they would materially affect conclusions. If H7 validation fails, downgrade H7 from active accepted to unresolved/reject and consider whether rare-subgroup WRN claim is dataset-specific noise. Future exploration can still include screen technical variables, culture/lineage subtype, or other untested predictors, but causality and generalizability remain outside the present evidence.",
