  "narrative": "All returned estimates are already signed to the registered hypothesis direction, so positive values support the claim and negative values oppose it. Using an approximate absolute 10% outcome-mean scale for clinical significance, H50 (MSI-high effect on dependency_WRN within adherent culture) has a very large signed estimate of +0.813 with 95% CI +0.780 to +0.846, far above the relevant WRN threshold and with adequate cells; I accept it as a dataset-specific refinement supporting the robust overall MSI-high/WRN association. H51 (PTEN-loss effect on dependency_STAT3 within Avana library) has estimate +0.288, CI +0.232 to +0.343, also robustly clinically meaningful and consistent with the validated main PTEN-loss/STAT3 effect; I accept and close it. H52 (PTEN-loss/STAT3 within non-Avana library) has point +0.092, but the interval is wide (-0.062 to +0.246) and the exposed non-Avana cell has only 27 samples; this is too unstable to accept or reject, so I defer it. The remaining new comparisons provide no reliable evidence for clinically meaningful claimed associations. H53 has point +0.0039 and upper bound +0.0251, essentially below the POLR2A clinical scale. H54 has point +0.0154 and interval -0.0216 to +0.0525; it does not support the claimed RB1-loss/WRN effect, although the interval is not an equivalence bound. H55 has a signed estimate opposite to the claimed direction and upper bound below the STAT3 clinical threshold. H56, H57, and H58 are tiny or opposite-signed and their upper bounds do not establish 10% clinical effects. H59-H61 test lineage-subtype modification of the large accepted associations; all point estimates are small or opposite in sign and the intervals do not support meaningful adenocarcinoma-versus-non-adenocarcinoma modification of H6, H17, or H11. Given multiple unadjusted discovery tests, I reject these unsupported associations while noting that confidence intervals are not formal equivalence proof for every possible small or opposite effect. Given the currently unvalidated status and large discovery effect size of H6 (SMARCA4 loss versus SMARCA2 dependency), I request independent validation of H6 now. Pending that validation, H17 remains the next highest-priority accepted unvalidated association.",
