s tests whether the expected p53-loss effect on MDM2 dependency appears in a MYC-driven p53-pathway context. MYC amplification versus dependency_USP7 among TP53-loss lines tests whether MYC biology modifies the p53-loss-associated USP7 dependency. TP53 loss versus dependency_WRN among MSI-negative lines tests whether TP53 loss has an effect on WRN that is not simply a reflection of MSI co-occurrence. These are exploratory but interpretable. I reopened H1, H4, H8, and H9 as active because I registered refinements targeting them; this does not mean their main effects are accepted. All new comparisons are registered as unresolved before evidence. During later appraisal, I will accept only when the signed estimate and interval clearly exceed the ~10% clinical-significance scale, with adequate cells. For interactions, a positive signed estimate means the claimed effect is larger in the indicated subgroup than in the complement. For mean differences within subgroups, a positive signed estimate means the exposed group shows more support for the registered direction than the comparator. Validation priorities remain H51 and then H50 if possible; additional validation should be reserved for large new accepted context effects rather than small nulls.",
